ue ASCII IDs; nonempty for rejected/unknown/conflict, exact code checked only where design specifies it. Rationale, next_snapshot, constraints and allowed_result_codes are oracle metadata, never expected output keys.\",\n    \"record_digest\": \"If record is structurally hashed, full closed envelope digest; null when malformed. Cases without an explicit digest assert code/semantics, not an invented digest.\",\n    \"next_snapshot\": \"Separate reducer value; input unchanged. Compare exact snapshot when provided.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_notes\": [\n    \"V01-V05: actual frozen suite/capture separate\",\n    \"V06-V07: closed input, canonical bytes, typed refs, result-as-record, no operational authority\",\n    \"V08/D1-D2: pure reducer history/current, chronology, orphans and replay\",\n    \"V09: alias, command version/stage/effect boundaries\",\n    \"V10: independently supplied source closure/pin/budget\",\n    \"V11/V14/D4: stable logical key and cross-lineage predecessor, no real fencing\",\n    \"V12: modeled reviewer eligibility\",\n    \"V13/V15/D3: expected cases, target/artifact/issuer, positive/disconfirming/claim/readback/applicability\",\n    \"V16: future candidate, not evaluated in baseline calibration\",\n    \"Hostile text ingestion, actual native/caller/resource/host effects, production protocol floor, whole-candidate nonauthor and one-winner concurrency are outside detached model qualification; no empirical claims.\"\n  ],\n  \"wrapper_note\": \"Fixture inputs/operation labels and historical snapshot lists are custodian test data and evaluation metadata, not a proposed new record or candidate API.\"\n}\n","raw_hex_by_case":{"canonical-principal-fixture:a-engineer":"","canonical-principal-fixture:a-writer":"","canonical-principal-fixture:a-reviewer":"","canonical-principal-fixture:a-custodian":"","canonical-oracle-fixture:a-oracle":"